  "framing": "What-if re-score: the recorded live VLM outputs of the 2026-10-13 AMD Token Factory run, fused with the CPU detector (YOLO26s fine-tuned on RealWaste) through the current decision rules. No new model calls.",
  "scope": "component validation on public RealWaste images — not field data from a plant",
  "disclosure": "In-domain and optimistic. The detector was fine-tuned on RealWaste photos from the same sessions as these 80 held-out images (one item per frame on the same floor; the held-out images were excluded from training), and every detector threshold here was read off this same test set: there is no calibration split. It shows the fusion rules work as designed on these images, not that the detector works on a truck bed of mixed RDF. The VLM side carries the replay's own caveat: the decision rules were changed after the live run, using that run's data.",
  "llm_note": "The live rows recorded the LLM's gate outcome, not its text, so the replayed LLM result is rebuilt from the recorded manifest_crosscheck state with a fixed confidence of 0.95. That confidence only fills the ocr_confidence gate value, which has no threshold and never moves the verdict. The VLM prompt was not changed for this re-score; latency is not re-measured (no model was called).",
